In accordance with Apache 2.0 § 4(d), the SYMBIOTYC modifications are
documented in the commit history of this repository. The modifications
include, but are not limited to:

  1. Rebranding of user-facing strings (Codex / codex -> CY / cy).
  2. Removal of OpenAI-specific landing-page links from the TUI.
  3. A local Python bridge (packaging/macos/cy_bridge.py) that
     translates between the Responses API (used by this CLI) and the
     Chat Completions API (used by the configured upstream endpoint).
  4. A macOS .app bundle and a launcher shell script that resolves the
     end-user's API key from environment, auth file, keychain, or a
     one-shot prompt.
  5. Local tool execution (read_file, write_file, list_dir, shell_exec,
     glob_files) inside the bridge so the end-user can operate on
     files and the local filesystem without sending them upstream.

This product does NOT redistribute any language model weights,
training data, or proprietary runtime artifacts. The CLI is a
model-agnostic client: at install time the end user selects which
upstream provider to talk to (e.g. SYMBIOTYC Cloud, OpenRouter,
Anthropic, or a self-hosted endpoint). Each upstream provider's own
terms of service govern the model invocation; they are not affected
by this NOTICE or by the Apache 2.0 License.

